PR #1302  overall: bug_confirmed
Spec: mseccfg was ambiguously 'optional' — it exists iff a field-defining extension (Zkr/Smmpm/Zicfilp/Smepmp) is present; software misdetection leaves M-mode security enforcement unconfigured
  [BUG] include/sbi/riscv_encoding.h:727-740  CSR_MSECCFG (macro definitions)
      MSECCFG_MMWP (bit 1) is defined but never referenced by any .c file — the codebase treats mseccfg as Smepmp+Zkr-only. Missing field macros for Zicfilp's MLPE bit and Smnpm's pointer-masking bits mean these sub-extensions have no representation in the mseccfg field model, violating the clarified spec where mseccfg exists whenever any of Smepmp, Zkr, Smmpm, Zicfilp, or Smnpm is implemented.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c:176-180  mstatus_init
      Writes CSR_MSECCFG (csr_set SSEED, csr_clear USEED) gated solely on SBI_HART_EXT_ZKR via sbi_hart_has_extension(). Under the clarified spec, Zkr is a valid field-defining extension, so the gate is logically correct. However, no trap-probe validates that CSR_MSECCFG physically exists before the csr_set/csr_clear — if the ISA string falsely advertises Zkr without hardware mseccfg, these instructions will raise illegal-instruction traps. The __check_ext_csr infrastructure exists (line 634) but is not applied to mseccfg.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c:698-706  hart_detect_features
      Reads CSR_MSECCFG.MML at cold boot, gated on SBI_HART_EXT_SMEPMP. Under the clarified spec Smepmp⇒mseccfg equivalence holds correctly. However, the csr_read is executed without a prior trap-probe — if the ISA string falsely claims Smepmp, the csr_read will trap. Also noteworthy: this function runs before mstatus_init(), yet mstatus_init() also writes mseccfg. If Smepmp is present but Zkr is not, this read succeeds (mseccfg exists via Smepmp) but mstatus_init() will skip the Zkr-gated SSEED/USEED write. That is correct. But if Zkr is present and Smepmp is not, the SSEED/USEED write in mstatus_init() happens on an mseccfg that was never trap-probed.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_hart_pmp.c:135-139  sbi_hart_smepmp_configure
      Executes csr_set(CSR_MSECCFG, MSECCFG_RLB) unconditionally at entry to the Smepmp configure path. The path is reachable only after epmp_protection registration (line 336), which requires SBI_HART_EXT_SMEPMP, so the CSR is assumed present. Under the clarified spec this assumption is correct (Smepmp⇒mseccfg), but no independent CSR-existence probe guards this write — a false ISA claim would trap here.
