      SBI_HART_EXT_SMEPMP is the primary extension flag used as predicate for mseccfg CSR access in hart_detect_features() (line 704) and sbi_hart_smepmp_configure() (lines 135, 185). The flag is populated from the ISA string by fdt_helper.c with no CSR trap-probe. A false-positive (ISA string says 'smepmp' but hardware has no mseccfg) causes illegal-instruction traps; a false-negative silently disables Smepmp enforcement.
